  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nI'm trying to configure my own matrix home server  on EC2 Amazon Linux AMI and  it's have following packages \r\n\r\n1. Python 2.7.12\r\n2. pip 9.0.1 from /usr/lib/python2.7/dist-packages (python 2.7)\r\n3. bcrypt==3.1.3\r\n4. py-bcrypt==0.4\r\n\r\nwhen i execute  **Configuring synapse**   cmd\r\n\r\n    python -m synapse.app.homeserver \\\r\n    --server-name mydomainname \\\r\n    --config-path homeserver.yaml \\\r\n    --generate-config \\\r\n    --report-stats=yes\r\n\r\nbelow error throwing \r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR:root:Can't import 'bcrypt' which is part of 'py-bcrypt'\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/ec2-user/.synapse/local/lib/python2.7/dist-packages/synapse/python_dependencies.py\", line 104, in check_requirements\r\n    module = __import__(module_name)\r\nImportError: No module named bcrypt\r\nMissing Requirement: Can't import 'bcrypt' which is part of 'py-bcrypt'\r\nTo install run:\r\n    pip install --upgrade --force \"py-bcrypt\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nEven i tried the cmd **pip install --upgrade --force \"py-bcrypt\"**  same error throwing \r\n\r\nCan you please help on this?\r\n\r\nThanks & Regards,\r\n\r\nArun Iruthaya Thomas\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
